            <div class="d-flex"> <img src="~/Images/career_related.png" alt="IB CP Logo" class="mx-3"> <h1 class="main-title">The IB Career-related Programme (CP)</h1></div>
            <p class="mt-5">Mount Litera School International is a candidate school* for the career-related programme. The school is pursuing authorisation as an IB World School. These are schools that share a common philosophy, a commitment to high-quality, challenging, international education that MLSI believes is important for our students.</p>
            <p>*Only schools authorised by the IB organisation can offer any of its four academic programmes: the Primary Years Programme (PYP), the Middle Years Programme (MYP), the Diploma Programme (DP), or the Career-related Programme (CP).</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Programme Info Box -->
        <div class="content-box">
            <h4><strong>The IB Career-related Programme (CP)</strong></h4>
            <h6><em>Where Academic Knowledge Meets Real-World Skills</em></h6>
            <p>The IB Career-related Programme (CP) is a unique educational framework designed for students aged 16–19 who wish to engage in academic learning while gaining practical skills and real-world experience. By combining at least two IB Diploma Programme (DP) subjects with career-related studies and a strong core framework, the CP offers a flexible and holistic learning model that prepares students for higher education, apprenticeships, or direct entry into the workforce.</p>
            <p>The CP core, comprising reflective projects, personal and professional skills, language and cultural studies, and community engagement, encourages students to become ethical, reflective, and global-minded individuals. Through this integrated approach, students explore real-life challenges, engage with local and global communities, and build transferable skills such as critical thinking, collaboration, communication, and ethical decision-making.</p>
            <p>Career-related studies offer hands-on, industry-relevant experience, bridging the gap between theory and practical application. The CP cultivates learners who are adaptable, self-directed, and equipped to succeed in a rapidly evolving, interconnected world.</p>
        </div>

